# Livong — AI Coding Rules

Livong is a roommate / shared-living platform. Monorepo: Go backend + Next.js frontend + PostgreSQL.

## Project Structure

```
apps/backend/         Go 1.26, Gin, raw SQL, JWT auth        (:8080)
apps/admin-backend/   Admin API, separate Go module          (:8081)
apps/web/             Next.js 16, React 19, TS, Tailwind v4  (:3000)
apps/admin/           Admin panel, Next.js                   (:3100)
docs/                 PRD, Architecture, API, DB Schema
cli.mjs               Cross-platform dev CLI (./livong)
```

## Hard Constraints (NEVER violate)

- **No new dependencies** without explicit approval. Stack is intentionally minimal.
- **No ORMs.** Raw SQL with `$1, $2` parameterized queries only.
- **No UI libraries.** No shadcn, Chakra, Radix, MUI. Tailwind + custom utility classes only.
- **No state libraries.** No Redux, Zustand, Jotai. React Context only.
- **No icon libraries.** Inline SVGs with `stroke="currentColor"`.
- **pnpm only.** Never `npm` or `yarn`.
- **No new top-level directories.** Everything goes under `apps/`, `docs/`, or `.github/`.

---

## Theme System (CRITICAL — most violations happen here)

Colors are CSS variables in `apps/web/src/app/globals.css`. Components use **semantic Tailwind classes** that auto-switch light/dark.

### NEVER write

```tsx
<div className="dark:bg-neutral-900">         // ❌ no dark: prefix
<div className="bg-[#525252]">                // ❌ no hex
<div className="text-neutral-500">            // ❌ neutral-* for theming
<div className="text-red-500 bg-red-100">     // ❌ raw colors for status
```

### ALWAYS write

```tsx
<div className="bg-surface text-foreground border border-border">
<p className="text-muted">Subtle text</p>
<button className="btn-primary">Click</button>
<div className="bg-error-surface text-error">Error message</div>
<div className="bg-success-surface text-success-text">Success</div>
```

### Token cheat sheet

| Need | Class |
|---|---|
| Page background | `bg-background` |
| Card / panel | `bg-surface` or `bg-surface-alt` |
| Primary action bg | `bg-primary` |
| Main text | `text-foreground` |
| Secondary text | `text-secondary` |
| Muted text | `text-muted` / `text-dim` / `text-faint` |
| Border | `border-border` or `border-border-light` |
| Error | `bg-error-surface text-error` |
| Success | `bg-success-surface text-success-text` |
| Warning | `bg-warning-surface text-warning` |
| Info | `bg-info-surface text-info` |

**Allowed exception:** `bg-neutral-900 text-white` for avatar circles only.

**Adding a new color:** update **all three** in `globals.css` — `:root`, `.dark`, AND `@theme inline`.

---

## Frontend (apps/web/) — Patterns

### Page skeleton (use this exact shape)

```tsx
"use client";

import { useEffect, useState } from "react";
import { useAuth } from "@/lib/auth";
import { api } from "@/lib/api";

export default function MyPage() {
  const { token, isAuthenticated, hydrated } = useAuth();
  const [data, setData] = useState<MyType[]>([]);

  useEffect(() => {
    if (!hydrated || !isAuthenticated) return;
    api.get<MyType[]>("/endpoint", token).then(setData);
  }, [hydrated, isAuthenticated, token]);

  return (
    <div className="page-container">
      <h1 className="text-foreground">Title</h1>
      {/* content */}
    </div>
  );
}
```

### Rules

- **Always** `"use client"` at top, `export default function PageName()`.
- **Always** import from `@/` (maps to `src/`).
- **Always** call API through `lib/api.ts`. Never raw `fetch()`.
- Types in `lib/types.ts`. Constants in `lib/constants.ts` with `as const`.
- Auth: `useAuth()` → `{ token, userId, isAuthenticated, hydrated }`. Wait for `hydrated` before redirects.
- Theme: `useTheme()` → `{ theme, toggle }`.
- Icons: inline SVG, `stroke="currentColor"`, color via parent text class.
- Utility classes: `.btn-primary`, `.btn-secondary`, `.card`, `.input`, `.page-container`.
- Animations: `.animate-fade-in-up`, `.animate-slide-in`, `.stagger`.
- Responsive: mobile-first. `md:` (≥768) and `lg:` (≥1024) breakpoints.
- Navigation: `AppShell.tsx` — sidebar on desktop, bottom nav on mobile.

---

## Backend (apps/backend/) — Patterns

### Handler skeleton (use this exact shape)

```go
// apps/backend/internal/rooms/handler.go
package rooms

import (
	"database/sql"
	"net/http"

	"github.com/gin-gonic/gin"
)

type Handler struct {
	db *sql.DB
}

func NewHandler(db *sql.DB) *Handler {
	return &Handler{db: db}
}

func (h *Handler) Create(c *gin.Context) {
	var req struct {
		Title string `json:"title" binding:"required"`
	}
	if err := c.ShouldBindJSON(&req); err != nil {
		c.JSON(http.StatusBadRequest, gin.H{"error": "Invalid request"})
		return
	}

	userId := c.GetString("userId")

	var id string
	err := h.db.QueryRow(
		`INSERT INTO rooms (title, user_id) VALUES ($1, $2) RETURNING id`,
		req.Title, userId,
	).Scan(&id)
	if err != nil {
		c.JSON(http.StatusInternalServerError, gin.H{"error": "Failed to create room"})
		return
	}

	c.JSON(http.StatusCreated, gin.H{"id": id})
}
```

### Route registration (in `main.go`)

```go
// Public group
public := r.Group("/api")
public.POST("/auth/login", authHandler.Login)

// Protected group (JWT middleware)
protected := r.Group("/api")
protected.Use(middleware.AuthRequired(jwtSecret))
protected.POST("/rooms", roomsHandler.Create)
```

### Rules

- **One `handler.go` per feature** in `internal/{feature}/`.
- Request: inline anonymous struct + `c.ShouldBindJSON(&req)`.
- Response: `c.JSON(statusCode, gin.H{...})`.
- Errors: `gin.H{"error": "Human message"}`. **Never** expose internals (`err.Error()`).
- Auth: `c.GetString("userId")` from middleware.
- SQL: `$1, $2` parameterized. **Never** concatenate strings into SQL.
- DB columns: `snake_case`. JSON keys: `camelCase`.
- Tables: plural, UUID PK, `CURRENT_TIMESTAMP` defaults.
- Migrations: append to `internal/database/migrations.go`, always `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS`.
- Routes: register in `main.go` under public or protected group.

---

## Decision Tree (when unsure, follow this)

- **New page?** → `apps/web/src/app/<route>/page.tsx`, use page skeleton above.
- **New component?** → `apps/web/src/components/`, theme tokens only.
- **New API endpoint?** → new feature dir under `apps/backend/internal/<feature>/`, handler skeleton, register route in `main.go`.
- **New DB table?** → migration in `internal/database/migrations.go`, plural name, UUID PK.
- **API surface changed?** → update `docs/api.md`.
- **Schema changed?** → update `docs/db-schema.md`.
- **Architecture changed?** → update `docs/architecture.md`.
- **Need a color?** → use a token. If no token fits, add one to all three places in `globals.css`.
- **Need an icon?** → inline SVG with `stroke="currentColor"`. Don't install a library.
- **Need a form?** → controlled `useState` + handler. No form library.
- **Need a date utility?** → native `Date` / `Intl.DateTimeFormat`. No `date-fns`/`dayjs`.

---

## Code Style

- No comments / docstrings unless logic is non-obvious.
- No premature abstractions. Three similar lines beats a bad helper.
- One concern per file. Files focused, not god-classes.
- Match existing patterns in the file you're editing.

## Running things

Always prefer `./livong` over raw commands:

```
./livong start       # backend + web
./livong status      # what's running
./livong fresh       # clean + install + start
./livong web:dev
./livong server:start
./livong admin:dev
```
